---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site, localBusinessSchema } from '../../config/site';

const procedureSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "MedicalProcedure",
  "name": "Damon™ Smile",
  "description": "Passive self-ligating braces designed to reduce friction and pressure throughout treatment.",
  "procedureType": "https://schema.org/Therapeutic",
  "provider": {
    "@type": "Dentist",
    "name": "Chang Orthodontics",
    "address": {
      "@type": "PostalAddress",
      "addressLocality": "Los Alamitos"
    }
  }
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`Damon Smile Los Alamitos | ${site.name}`}
  description="Passive self-ligating braces designed to reduce friction and pressure throughout treatment."
  schema={[localBusinessSchema, procedureSchema]}
>
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16 md:py-24">
    <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-brand-primary mb-4">
      <a href="/services" class="hover:underline">Services</a>
    </p>
    <h1 class="font-serif text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-neutral-dark mb-4 leading-tight">
      Damon™ Smile
    </h1>
    <p class="text-xl text-neutral-mid mb-8 leading-relaxed">
      Passive self-ligating braces designed to reduce friction and pressure throughout treatment.
    </p>
    <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none text-neutral-mid leading-relaxed">
      <p class="mb-4">Chang Orthodontics offers passive self-ligating Damon Smile braces as an alternative to conventional metal braces. Instead of using elastic ties or metal ligatures to hold the archwire in place, Damon braces use a built-in slide mechanism that allows the wire to move more freely. The result is lighter, more continuous forces on the teeth — and for most patients, fewer office visits compared to traditional braces.</p>
      <p class="mb-4">If you're considering orthodontic treatment in Los Alamitos and want an option that minimizes friction and reduces the number of adjustment appointments, Damon Smile is worth understanding in detail.</p>
      <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-semibold text-neutral-dark mt-8 mb-4">How Damon Smile Braces Work</h2>
      <p class="mb-4">Traditional braces require elastic ties — the small colored bands wrapped around each bracket — to hold the archwire in position. Those ties grip the wire tightly, creating friction and requiring regular replacement as they stretch and degrade over time.</p>
      <p class="mb-4">Damon brackets eliminate the tie entirely. A small door or "slide" built into each bracket closes over the archwire and holds it passively. Because there's no elastic pressing against the wire, the wire can respond more naturally to tooth movement. This passive self-ligation reduces the friction between the bracket and wire, which is the key mechanical difference from conventional braces.</p>
      <p class="mb-4">Lower friction generally means the teeth move with less force — not no force, but gentler, more consistent pressure over time rather than bursts of higher pressure at each tightening appointment.</p>
      <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-semibold text-neutral-dark mt-8 mb-4">What to Expect During Treatment</h2>
      <p class="mb-4">At your initial consultation, Dr. Chang will evaluate your bite, spacing, and alignment to determine whether Damon Smile is appropriate for your case. Not every alignment issue has one single best solution, so this visit is about matching the treatment to your specific needs.</p>
      <p class="mb-4">If you move forward with Damon braces, the bonding appointment — where the brackets are attached to the teeth — typically takes about an hour to an hour and a half. The archwire is threaded through each bracket and secured using the slide mechanism rather than tied in with elastics.</p>
      <p class="mb-4">Follow-up appointments at Chang Orthodontics are generally scheduled less frequently than with traditional braces, because there are no elastics to replace. Visits typically focus on checking progress, switching archwires as treatment advances, and making any needed adjustments. Many patients find this reduced appointment frequency easier to fit around school or work schedules.</p>
      <p class="mb-4">Overall treatment length varies depending on the complexity of your case. Mild spacing or crowding issues may resolve more quickly than significant bite corrections. Dr. Chang can give you a more specific timeline estimate after reviewing your records.</p>
      <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-semibold text-neutral-dark mt-8 mb-4">Appearance and Comfort</h2>
      <p class="mb-4">Damon Smile brackets are designed with a lower profile than many conventional brackets, which some patients find more comfortable against the inside of the lips and cheeks. The system is available in metal and, for patients who prefer a less visible option, clear ceramic brackets that blend more closely with tooth color.</p>
      <p class="mb-4">Mild soreness in the first few days after placement and after wire changes is normal. Over-the-counter pain relievers and soft foods during those windows typically manage discomfort well.</p>
      <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-semibold text-neutral-dark mt-8 mb-4">Who Is a Good Candidate</h2>
      <p class="mb-4">Damon Smile can treat a broad range of orthodontic issues — crowding, spacing, overbites, underbites, and crossbites among them. It's used in both adolescent and adult patients. The best way to know whether it suits your situation is a consultation where your bite and alignment are evaluated directly.</p>
      <p class="mb-4">Patients in Los Alamitos who are considering braces for the first time, or who have had braces before and are looking at retreatment, can ask about Damon Smile as part of that initial conversation.</p>
      <p class="mb-4">---</p>
      <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-semibold text-neutral-dark mt-8 mb-4">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <p class="mb-4">**Are Damon braces faster than traditional braces?** Treatment time depends on the complexity of each case, not just the bracket type. The passive self-ligation can allow efficient tooth movement, but there's no universal guarantee of a shorter timeline. Dr. Chang will give you a case-specific estimate at your consultation.</p>
      <p class="mb-4">**Do Damon braces hurt more or less than regular braces?** Most patients report similar levels of initial soreness. The lighter forces used in passive self-ligation mean some patients find ongoing discomfort more manageable, but individual experiences vary.</p>
      <p class="mb-4">**Do I still need to come in for adjustments?** Yes, but typically less often. Because there are no elastics to replace, appointments are generally spaced further apart than with conventional braces.</p>
      <p class="mb-4">**Are clear Damon brackets available?** Yes. Damon Smile offers a clear ceramic bracket option for patients who prefer a less noticeable look while still using the self-ligating system.</p>
      <p class="mb-4">**How do I clean my teeth with Damon braces?** Brushing and flossing technique is similar to other braces — you'll want to clean around each bracket and under the archwire carefully. Dr. Chang's team will walk you through the specifics at your bonding appointment.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-10 flex gap-4 flex-wrap">
      <a href="/schedule" class="btn-primary">Schedule a Consultation</a>
      <a href="/services" class="btn-secondary">View All Services</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
